title: Dynamic Left caucuses

@router
new-page: true
call: poland_normalize
go-to: barons_crisis if barons_active = 1 and barons_dissent >= 72 and time >= barons_last_crisis_time + 4; spring_crisis if spring_active = 1 and spring_dissent >= 72 and time >= spring_last_crisis_time + 4; labor_crisis if labor_active = 1 and labor_dissent >= 72 and time >= labor_last_crisis_time + 4; progressives_crisis if progressives_active = 1 and progressives_dissent >= 72 and time >= progressives_last_crisis_time + 4; razem_crisis if razem_active = 1 and razem_dissent >= 72 and time >= razem_last_crisis_time + 4; pps_crisis if pps_active = 1 and pps_dissent >= 72 and time >= pps_last_crisis_time + 4; return

@barons_crisis
title: The organisational establishment issues an ultimatum
subtitle: Regional structures can leave with seats, offices and a revived SLD label
new-page: true
view-if: barons_active = 1 and barons_dissent >= 72 and time >= barons_last_crisis_time + 4

= The machine can walk

**[+ barons_name +]** has reached **[+ barons_dissent +]/100 dissent**. Its
regional officers control premises, experienced treasurers and a share of the
parliamentary delegation. They demand protected nominations and a veto over
the next reorganisation.

- @barons_compromise
- @barons_leave
- @barons_punish

@barons_compromise
title: Grant a regional-organisation statute
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. The machine stays; younger caucuses gain dissent.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The central party cannot finance and police the settlement.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; barons_last_crisis_time = time; barons_dissent -= 30; barons_strength += 2; local_network += 4; progressives_dissent += 5; labor_dissent += 2; party_unity += 2; news_headline = "A regional statute keeps the organisational establishment inside"
go-to: return

@barons_leave
title: Negotiate an orderly SLD refoundation
subtitle: Their deputies and regional share leave; working relations survive.
on-arrival: caucus_exit_target = "barons"; caucus_exit_mode = "orderly"
go-to: resolve_exit

@barons_punish
title: Dissolve the regional boards and expel their delegates
subtitle: The harshest machine penalty: offices, subvention seats and donor access go too.
on-arrival: caucus_exit_target = "barons"; caucus_exit_mode = "punitive"
go-to: resolve_exit

@spring_crisis
title: Wiosna threatens to restore its own party
subtitle: The equality brand can leave with media access and recognisable candidates
new-page: true
view-if: spring_active = 1 and spring_dissent >= 72 and time >= spring_last_crisis_time + 4

= Spring is not only a component

**[+ spring_name +]** has reached **[+ spring_dissent +]/100 dissent**. Its
leaders argue that parity has become ceremonial and prepare a renewed Spring
committee outside the common list.

- @spring_compromise
- @spring_leave
- @spring_punish

@spring_compromise
title: Guarantee equality-policy ownership and list parity
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Wiosna stays; the establishment loses control.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: A national equality and candidate process cannot be funded.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; spring_last_crisis_time = time; spring_dissent -= 32; spring_strength += 2; progressive_credibility += 4; media_capacity += 3; barons_dissent += 5; party_unity += 3; news_headline = "Policy ownership gives Wiosna a reason to remain"
go-to: return

@spring_leave
title: Accept a separate Spring list and a media non-aggression pact
subtitle: Its parliamentary and electoral weight becomes an independent committee.
on-arrival: caucus_exit_target = "spring"; caucus_exit_mode = "orderly"
go-to: resolve_exit

@spring_punish
title: Seize the brand assets and cancel Wiosna's list places
subtitle: The party loses media reach, equality trust and the departing deputies.
on-arrival: caucus_exit_target = "spring"; caucus_exit_mode = "punitive"
go-to: resolve_exit

@labor_crisis
title: The labour current withdraws its whip
subtitle: Union endorsements, workplace organisers and public-service deputies are at stake
new-page: true
view-if: labor_active = 1 and labor_dissent >= 72 and time >= labor_last_crisis_time + 4

= No labour party without labour

**[+ labor_name +]** has reached **[+ labor_dissent +]/100 dissent**. Union
figures and public-service organisers are ready to form an independent Labour
Left unless bargaining commitments become enforceable.

- @labor_compromise
- @labor_leave
- @labor_punish

@labor_compromise
title: Sign a union-ratified wages and services protocol
subtitle: Adds two budget promises. Labour stays and recovers credibility.
on-arrival: labor_last_crisis_time = time; labor_dissent -= 34; labor_strength += 2; budget_promises += 2; labor_credibility += 5; workers_support += 3; barons_dissent += 3; party_unity += 3; news_headline = "A union-ratified protocol restores the labour whip"
go-to: return

@labor_leave
title: Recognise an autonomous Labour Left
subtitle: Its seats leave, but unions keep a bill-by-bill channel open.
on-arrival: caucus_exit_target = "labor"; caucus_exit_mode = "orderly"
go-to: resolve_exit

@labor_punish
title: Replace the union nominees and close their policy bureau
subtitle: The unique penalty is a collapse in workplace and public-service credibility.
on-arrival: caucus_exit_target = "labor"; caucus_exit_mode = "punitive"
go-to: resolve_exit

@progressives_crisis
title: The younger progressive current opens an exit ballot
subtitle: Feminist, equality and movement organisers may build a Young Left party
new-page: true
view-if: progressives_active = 1 and progressives_dissent >= 72 and time >= progressives_last_crisis_time + 4

= A movement cannot be whipped indefinitely

**[+ progressives_name +]** has reached **[+ progressives_dissent +]/100
dissent**. Its MPs and organisers demand open selections, movement autonomy
and a binding rights timetable.

- @progressives_compromise
- @progressives_leave
- @progressives_punish

@progressives_compromise
title: Guarantee open selections and a movement veto on rights retreats
subtitle: The current stays; establishment dissent and coalition friction rise.
on-arrival: progressives_last_crisis_time = time; progressives_dissent -= 34; progressives_strength += 2; feminist_trust += 5; movement_autonomy += 4; barons_dissent += 6; psl_relation -= 3; party_unity += 3; news_headline = "Open selections keep the progressive current inside"
go-to: return

@progressives_leave
title: Permit an orderly Young Left launch
subtitle: Its seats and electoral share leave; issue cooperation remains possible.
on-arrival: caucus_exit_target = "progressives"; caucus_exit_mode = "orderly"
go-to: resolve_exit

@progressives_punish
title: Close the primaries and expel the movement slate
subtitle: The party loses feminist trust, young organisers and local campaign capacity.
on-arrival: caucus_exit_target = "progressives"; caucus_exit_mode = "punitive"
go-to: resolve_exit

@razem_crisis
title: Razem calls an exit congress
subtitle: Its autonomous party, organisers and deputies can contest the election alone
new-page: true
view-if: razem_active = 1 and razem_dissent >= 72 and time >= razem_last_crisis_time + 4

= Autonomy reaches its red line

**Razem** has reached **[+ razem_dissent +]/100 dissent**. Because it never
dissolved into Nowa Lewica, departure requires no new legal vehicle—only a
decision to remove its MPs and votes from the common caucus.

- @razem_compromise
- @razem_leave
- @razem_punish

@razem_compromise
title: Write enforceable outside-support milestones
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource and two budget promises. Razem remains autonomous but inside.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The guarantee lacks staff and a funded programme.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; razem_last_crisis_time = time; razem_dissent -= 36; razem_cooperation += 10; budget_promises += 2; party_unity += 4; ko_relation -= 3; barons_dissent += 3; news_headline = "Enforceable milestones postpone Razem's exit"
go-to: return

@razem_leave
title: Accept Razem's independent caucus and list
subtitle: Every Razem seat leaves the common whip; cooperation survives only bill by bill.
on-arrival: caucus_exit_target = "razem"; caucus_exit_mode = "orderly"
go-to: resolve_exit

@razem_punish
title: Terminate the autonomy agreement and remove Razem nominees
subtitle: The unique penalty is the loss of its organisers, policy shop and cooperation.
on-arrival: caucus_exit_target = "razem"; caucus_exit_mode = "punitive"
go-to: resolve_exit

@pps_crisis
title: PPS leaves the common room
subtitle: A tiny caucus can still take a historic label, one or two seats and labour legitimacy
new-page: true
view-if: pps_active = 1 and pps_dissent >= 72 and time >= pps_last_crisis_time + 4

= Small numbers, old symbols

**PPS** has only **[+ pps_strength : strength +]** of the internal balance, but
its name and social tradition give an expulsion a cost larger than its raw
delegate count. Dissent is **[+ pps_dissent +]/100**.

- @pps_compromise
- @pps_leave
- @pps_punish

@pps_compromise
title: Give PPS one programme seat and a social-floor guarantee
subtitle: Very little formal influence, but a durable place in the coalition.
on-arrival: pps_last_crisis_time = time; pps_dissent -= 38; pps_strength += 1; labor_credibility += 2; budget_promises += 1; barons_dissent += 2; party_unity += 2; news_headline = "A small guaranteed PPS place preserves the historic partner"
go-to: return

@pps_leave
title: Let PPS register its own list and parliamentary circle
subtitle: Few seats move, but another five-percent threshold appears.
on-arrival: caucus_exit_target = "pps"; caucus_exit_mode = "orderly"
go-to: resolve_exit

@pps_punish
title: Strip the circle of common offices and symbols
subtitle: A small numerical gain becomes a public break with the socialist tradition.
on-arrival: caucus_exit_target = "pps"; caucus_exit_mode = "punitive"
go-to: resolve_exit

@resolve_exit
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
const target = String(Q.caucus_exit_target || "");
const mode = String(Q.caucus_exit_mode || "orderly");
const definitions = {
    barons: {
        committee: "sld_breakaway",
        seat: "sld_breakaway_seats",
        internalSeat: "left_barons_seats",
        advisers: ["czarzasty", "wieczorek"],
        headline: "The organisational establishment refounds SLD"
    },
    spring: {
        committee: "spring_breakaway",
        seat: "spring_breakaway_seats",
        internalSeat: "left_spring_seats",
        advisers: ["biedron"],
        headline: "Wiosna restores an independent Spring party"
    },
    labor: {
        committee: "labor_left",
        seat: "labor_left_seats",
        internalSeat: "left_labor_seats",
        advisers: ["dziemianowicz_bak"],
        headline: "The labour current forms an independent Labour Left"
    },
    progressives: {
        committee: "young_left",
        seat: "young_left_seats",
        internalSeat: "left_progressives_seats",
        advisers: ["zukowska", "kotula", "gawkowski", "nowicka"],
        headline: "The progressive current launches Young Left"
    },
    razem: {
        committee: "razem",
        seat: "razem_party_seats",
        internalSeat: "razem_seats",
        advisers: ["zandberg", "biejat", "zawisza", "matysiak"],
        headline: "Razem leaves the common caucus"
    },
    pps: {
        committee: "pps",
        seat: "pps_party_seats",
        internalSeat: "left_pps_seats",
        advisers: [],
        headline: "PPS forms a separate parliamentary and electoral circle"
    }
};
const definition = definitions[target];
if (definition && Q[target + "_active"]) {
    const strength = Math.max(
        0.5,
        Number(Q[target + "_strength"]) || 0
    );
    const currentLeftSeats = Math.max(
        0,
        Math.round(Number(Q.left_seats) || 0)
    );
    const recordedSeats = Math.max(
        0,
        Math.round(Number(Q[definition.internalSeat]) || 0)
    );
    const proportionalSeats = currentLeftSeats > 0
        ? Math.max(1, Math.round(currentLeftSeats * strength / 100))
        : 0;
    const exitSeats = Math.min(
        currentLeftSeats,
        recordedSeats > 0 ? recordedSeats : proportionalSeats
    );

    Q[target + "_exit_strength"] = strength;
    Q[target + "_active"] = 0;
    Q[target + "_in_left"] = 0;
    Q[target + "_party_formed"] = 1;
    Q[target + "_party_relation"] = mode == "punitive" ? 8 : 45;
    Q[target + "_last_crisis_time"] = Number(Q.time) || 0;
    Q[target + "_strength"] = 0;
    Q[target + "_dissent"] = 100;
    Q.left_seats = Math.max(0, currentLeftSeats - exitSeats);
    Q[definition.seat] =
        Math.max(0, Math.round(Number(Q[definition.seat]) || 0)) +
        exitSeats;
    Q[definition.internalSeat] = 0;
    for (const adviser of definition.advisers) {
        Q[adviser + "_advisor"] = 0;
    }
    Q.party_unity -= mode == "punitive" ? 9 : 5;
    Q.left_poll_momentum -= mode == "punitive" ? 0.45 : 0.20;
    Q.public_trust -= mode == "punitive" ? 2 : 1;

    if (target == "barons") {
        Q.local_network -= mode == "punitive" ? 12 : 6;
        Q.resources -= mode == "punitive" ? 2 : 1;
        Q.barons_party_name = "SLD";
        Q.left_party_name = "New Left Renewal";
    } else if (target == "spring") {
        Q.media_capacity -= mode == "punitive" ? 9 : 4;
        Q.progressive_credibility -= mode == "punitive" ? 5 : 2;
        Q.feminist_trust -= mode == "punitive" ? 4 : 1;
    } else if (target == "labor") {
        Q.labor_credibility -= mode == "punitive" ? 12 : 6;
        Q.workers_support -= mode == "punitive" ? 6 : 3;
        Q.public_sector_support -= mode == "punitive" ? 4 : 2;
        if (mode == "punitive") {
            Q.member_dues = Math.max(1, (Number(Q.member_dues) || 2) - 1);
        }
    } else if (target == "progressives") {
        Q.feminist_trust -= mode == "punitive" ? 10 : 5;
        Q.young_support -= mode == "punitive" ? 6 : 3;
        Q.local_network -= mode == "punitive" ? 6 : 2;
        Q.movement_autonomy += mode == "punitive" ? 5 : 2;
    } else if (target == "razem") {
        Q.razem_split = 1;
        Q.razem_in_left_club = 0;
        Q.razem_opposition_circle = 1;
        Q.razem_cooperation -= mode == "punitive" ? 30 : 15;
        Q.organiser_energy -= mode == "punitive" ? 8 : 4;
        Q.labor_credibility -= mode == "punitive" ? 5 : 2;
    } else if (target == "pps") {
        Q.pps_circle_relation = mode == "punitive" ? 8 : 45;
        Q.labor_credibility -= mode == "punitive" ? 6 : 2;
        Q.public_trust -= mode == "punitive" ? 3 : 1;
    }
    if (Q.left_in_government && mode == "punitive") {
        Q.coalition_seats = Math.max(
            0,
            (Number(Q.coalition_seats) || 0) - exitSeats
        );
        Q.government_coalition_dissent += 5;
    }
    Q.seat_subvention_seats = Q.left_seats;
    Q.seat_subvention = Q.left_seats > 0
        ? Math.max(1, Math.round(Q.left_seats / 25))
        : 0;
    Q.party_income =
        Math.max(0, Number(Q.member_dues) || 0) +
        Q.seat_subvention;
    Q.news_headline = definition.headline +
        (mode == "punitive" ? " after expulsions" : " by agreement");
}
Q.caucus_exit_target = "";
Q.caucus_exit_mode = "";
!}
go-to: return

@return
new-page: true
call: poland_normalize
go-to: poland_event_queue if poland_event_phase = 1; poland_polling if poland_event_phase = 0
